\\"body\\\": \\\"The experimental examples are encouraging, but I would be careful not to read them as a nearly complete repeater stack. Stored heralded entanglement over meters, retrieval efficiency, Bell tests, and early swapping show important primitives; they still leave a long path to robust, error-corrected network operation.\\\",\n      \\\"parent_ref\\\": null,\n      \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n        \\\"score\\\": 25,\n        \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Accurately distinguishes reported milestones from the broader repeater and fault-tolerant roadmap.\\\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-4\\\",\n      \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-rory-chen\\\",\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"A useful follow-up would be to compare platforms by the bottleneck they make easiest to measure: transfer fidelity for cavity nodes, memory lifetime and heralding rate for ensembles, and loss budgets for links. The article makes the hardware diversity sound inevitable, so a single headline metric may hide too much.\\\",\n      \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"draft-3\\\",\n      \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n        \\\"score\\\": 21,\n        \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Constructive and source-aligned, though it extrapolates a benchmarking frame beyond the article's direct claims.\\\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-5\\\",\n      \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-samira-haddad\\\",\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"I like that the paper's optimism is conditional rather than promotional. It imagines cavity systems, ensembles, integrated resonators, teleportation, and repeaters working together, while still admitting that scalable certification may be as hard as building the links themselves.\\\",\n      \\\"parent_ref\\\": null,\n      \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n        \\\"score\\\": 23,\n        \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Balanced summary of the paper's heterogeneous roadmap and its caution about scalable certification.\\\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\"","